  "body": "Stacked on #1064 (branch `issue/904-reduced-fidelity-laws`: this uses its `verify/excess.rs` split and its `coarse_contain` fixture). Fork synced at v0.18.0.\n\n## Root cause\n\nA Z drill, bore or thread mill verifies (`Mode::Boundary`) against rim loops that are our own polygons of each hole's declared circle (`material_source::rim_loop`), built to `RIM_SAG_BUDGET` = 0.005 mm, half the 0.01 mm `GOUGE_TOL`. A 2 mm rim (48 sides) stands 0.00428 mm inside its circle, so a matched drill reads `r - 0.00428` off it. #864 had law (b) read **every** loop at `GOUGE_TOL - excess`. Past 0.01 - 0.00428 = 0.00572 mm of excess (a model flagged above ~0.0107 mm; the issue saw 0.0105 clean, 0.011 convicted) the tolerance left no longer covered the rim's own sagitta: `Gouge { at: 1 }` on a matched drill, and on every ring of a matched bore. Past 0.015 mm `excess_floor` reads untightened and the gate refuses by name, which is why 0.03 read clean.\n\n## What changed\n\n- `sim::verify::VerifyContext` gets `rims: &[(Point2, f64)]` (empty by default): the declared circles of a containment kind. `VerifyContext::is_rim` / `loop_tol` (in `verify/excess.rs`) match a loop to one (every vertex within 2 um: the region's 1 um lattice snap).\n- Law (b) (`verify/section.rs`), both the law-point reading and the Boundary whole-move wall reading, reads a rim loop at the plain `gouge_tol` and every other loop at `tightened(gouge_tol)` as before. Rims are found once per verify call.\n- `app::operation::generate` fills `rims` from the Drill (Z holes) and Bore params (Thread declares none, see below) when the depth law is `Contain` (`material_source::rims_of`), at both verify sites.\n- The solid law against the model's facets (`contain_into`) is untouched and still tightened.\n\nWhy the plain tolerance is honest: the excess measures how far a coarse model's facets stand inside its true surface; a rim is not a facet but a circle we draw from the hole's own centre and radius, so the rim's reading is exactly today's full-fidelity verdict. Nothing a full-fidelity model convicts is acquitted. Decision file: `docs/decisions/1057-drill-excess-false-gouge.md` (options dropped: finer rims, exact-circle reading, zeroing the excess for the containment kinds, recognising rims structurally in sim).\n\n## Readings (`coarse_rims` fixture: 40x40x20 block, 20x20 cavity blind at Z 10, DR-0400 to Z 10.2)\n\n| flagged | before | after |\n|---|---|---|\n| full, 0.008, 0.0105 | clean | clean |\n| 0.011, 0.012, 0.0149 | `Gouge { at: 1 }` | clean |\n| 0.03 | clean + refused by name | clean + refused by name |\n\nMatched bore (EM-0800-4FL in a 6 mm-radius hole) at 0.011 / 0.0149: before `Gouge { at: 6, 7, 8, 17, ... }`, after clean.\n\n## How tested\n\nPinning tests (all fail before the fix where they name a false conviction, pass after):\n- `coarse_rims::a_matched_drill_is_clean_on_a_model_flagged_anywhere_below_the_refusal_bound` (full, 0.008, 0.0105, 0.011, 0.012, 0.0149)\n- `coarse_rims::a_matched_bore_is_clean_near_the_refusal_bound` (+ a bore offset 1 mm into the wall still convicts at 0.0149)\n- `coarse_rims::the_real_drill_gouges_still_convict_on_a_model_near_the_refusal_bound` (oversize drill, drill offset into the wall, drill 0.5 mm past the floor - each at full, 0.011 and 0.0149; and 0.005 mm past the floor: clean at full fidelity, a gouge at 0.0149)\n- `coarse_rims::a_matched_drill_past_the_bound_is_refused_by_name_not_convicted` (0.03: no warnings, the gate's fidelity line by name)\n- `coarse_rims::a_thread_mill_on_a_coarse_model_is_never_read_looser_than_at_full_fidelity`\n- `model_excess::a_declared_rim_is_read_untightened_and_no_other_loop_is` (sim: an undeclared rim convicted near the bound, declared clean, a 2.01 drill still convicted, a declaration that does not trace the loop leaves the coarse boss convicted)\n\nGate: `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/issue/904-reduced-fidelity-laws` on the final head fe7403bc - sim 9 s, motion 4 s, app 201 s, 0 failed (3.6 min); plus `verify` and `mill2d_c` (rim law and bore/thread from stock) green; `cargo clippy -p camcraft-sim -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` clean. No goldens or snapshot PNGs moved.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- Thread declares no rim (#1073 review): since #1071 its region reads the major circle (`thread_rims::major_rims`), so a minor declaration traced no loop. A thread mill on a coarse model keeps the tightened reading (conservative) and may convict near the refusal bound where full fidelity is clean; declaring the major circle is a follow-up.\n- The 3+2 framed verify site passes the same rims; a rim drawn in the local frame that does not match the world-frame circles simply falls back to the tightened reading (today's behaviour). Not exercised by a framed fixture.\n\nChangelog: A drill or bore matched to its hole is no longer falsely convicted of a gouge on a model imported between ~0.0105 mm and the 0.015 mm refusal bound (#1057, PR #1073)\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #1057\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
